    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the Native Americans who called the area 'Long Island' because it was an island in 1872.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.phillipscountyks.org/departments/tourism/history-of-long-island"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Long Island was first settled in 1869 by Amos Cole, and many more settlers followed shortly after.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.phillipscountyks.org/departments/tourism/history-of-long-island"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1885 the railroad arrived, bringing more individuals and families back to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.phillipscountyks.org/departments/tourism/history-of-long-island"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A beautiful crop was produced in 1873, but the following year grasshoppers destroyed all vegetables, sending families back east.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.phillipscountyks.org/departments/tourism/history-of-long-island"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Soon new buildings, homes, and businesses were built all around as the town began to boom.",
